WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.321 --> 00:00:04.304
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.178
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is "believe",

00:00:07.178 --> 00:00:09.158
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:09.158 --> 00:00:11.249
all of the major problems in the world.

00:00:11.249 --> 00:00:13.690
So to help you on your journey
today we're want to talk

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.314
about how you can configure out

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.420
what you really, really want.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.267
Rule number four is my personal favorite,

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.151
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:23.358
And as always, as you're watching,

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:25.719
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:27.415
please leave it down the comments below,

00:00:27.415 --> 00:00:29.494
put quotes around it so that
other people can be inspired,

00:00:29.494 --> 00:00:31.298
you might win a prize too.

00:00:31.298 --> 00:00:32.602
And also when your write it down

00:00:32.602 --> 00:00:35.881
it's much more likely to
stick to yourself as well.

00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:36.714
Enjoy.

00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:40.167
(gentle music)

00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:53.160
(reflexive music)

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:56.036
- The point I want to share with you is,

00:00:56.036 --> 00:00:58.320
when I was growing up my
dad took out this poem

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.825
and he translated it from
Sanskrit into English,

00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:06.418
and it was a poem from the
Bengali poet Rabindranath Tagore.

00:01:06.418 --> 00:01:08.625
And allow me to share it with you,

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.423
it's simply said,:

00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:14.590
"Spring is past, summer has
gone and winter is here,

00:01:16.638 --> 00:01:19.427
"and the song I meant
to sing remains unsung,

00:01:19.427 --> 00:01:22.409
"for I've spent my days stringing

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:25.076
"and unstringing my instrument".

00:01:27.414 --> 00:01:29.506
And my brother and I used
to look at it every morning

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:32.049
before we go out to school but
I never really understood it,

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:33.605
so when I got a little older I said,

00:01:33.605 --> 00:01:37.603
"Dad, you know that poem you
had on our refrigerator door.

00:01:37.603 --> 00:01:40.210
"What was it all about?"

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.411
And my dad looked at me and he said,

00:01:41.411 --> 00:01:43.492
"Robin, that was a poem written by a man

00:01:43.492 --> 00:01:47.257
"whose heart was filled with
regret over a life half-lived".

00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:50.102
He said, "Robin, that was
a poem written by a man

00:01:50.102 --> 00:01:51.922
"who postponed his life.

00:01:51.922 --> 00:01:53.862
"He always wanted to do something special.

00:01:53.862 --> 00:01:55.757
"He always wanted to do important work.

00:01:55.757 --> 00:01:58.003
"He always wanted to
be loving in the world.

00:01:58.003 --> 00:01:59.699
"He always wanted to be creative.

00:01:59.699 --> 00:02:01.309
"He always wanted to see the world,

00:02:01.309 --> 00:02:03.726
"but he got busy being busy".

00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:08.364
Are you being busy being busy?

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:13.528
Have you lost that connection
to the life you wanted to live

00:02:13.528 --> 00:02:15.430
when you were a little kid?

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.417
Are you so busy stringing your instrument

00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.833
that the song that your
life was meant to sing

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:24.666
has died or is dormant within you?

00:02:25.638 --> 00:02:27.730
And my challenge to you is simply this:

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.624
to do whatever it takes
before you sleep tonight

00:02:30.624 --> 00:02:32.530
to reconnect with the best within you

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.098
that you may have lost.

00:02:34.098 --> 00:02:35.737
Because one of the things
I've noticed is this,

00:02:35.737 --> 00:02:38.927
there are too many amongst
us walking the planet today

00:02:38.927 --> 00:02:41.166
who are sort in awakened sleep,

00:02:41.166 --> 00:02:43.581
they have lost the sense
of who they truly are,

00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:46.144
and your life will never
work if there's a huge space

00:02:46.144 --> 00:02:47.841
between who you truly are

00:02:47.841 --> 00:02:50.002
and the person you know
you're meant to be.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.696
Your life will never
be flooded with energy,

00:02:52.696 --> 00:02:54.928
creative, productivity and happiness

00:02:54.928 --> 00:02:59.197
if there is a large space
between your life right now

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:01.058
and your unlived life.

00:03:01.058 --> 00:03:04.476
And my request and encouragement
and challenge to you

00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:07.314
is truly that you make things happen

00:03:07.314 --> 00:03:10.169
so that the person you
are starting tomorrow

00:03:10.169 --> 00:03:11.956
is more who you know you truly are.

00:03:11.956 --> 00:03:13.749
It makes me thing of George Bernard Shaw,

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:15.363
who was asked on his deathbed,

00:03:15.363 --> 00:03:18.029
"What would you do if you could
live your life over again?"

00:03:18.029 --> 00:03:21.775
And he replied, after a long pause,

00:03:21.775 --> 00:03:26.134
"I wish I could become the
person I know I was meant to be".

00:03:26.134 --> 00:03:29.774
And I suggest to you, it's
never too late for you to become

00:03:29.774 --> 00:03:33.014
the person you've always wanted to be.

00:03:33.014 --> 00:03:35.585
But don't postpone it for next year,

00:03:35.585 --> 00:03:37.971
don't postpone it for next month,

00:03:37.971 --> 00:03:40.531
start being that person, that human being,

00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:43.949
that creative force,
that business builder,

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:47.096
that mother or father, that athlete,

00:03:47.096 --> 00:03:50.768
that humanitarian, that force of good

00:03:50.768 --> 00:03:54.696
that you have always wanted
to be beginning right now.

00:03:54.696 --> 00:03:58.345
(reflexive music)

00:03:58.345 --> 00:03:59.856
- If you're familiar with my work you know

00:03:59.856 --> 00:04:03.380
for the last 34 years
I've been just obsessed

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.913
with wanting to know
what makes the difference

00:04:05.913 --> 00:04:07.809
in the quality of people's lives.

00:04:07.809 --> 00:04:09.503
Why is it so many people have big dreams

00:04:09.503 --> 00:04:11.339
but such a small number of people

00:04:11.339 --> 00:04:13.257
ever make those dreams a reality?

00:04:13.257 --> 00:04:14.811
And for those that do make it reality,

00:04:14.811 --> 00:04:17.650
what is it to gets them
not only to follow through

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.714
but then to enjoy what they have?

00:04:19.714 --> 00:04:20.939
I don't know if you've
ever had the experience

00:04:20.939 --> 00:04:23.455
of achieving something
that you've always wanted

00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:25.538
and then afterwards thinking to yourself,

00:04:25.538 --> 00:04:27.348
"Is this all there is?"

00:04:27.348 --> 00:04:28.571
It's one of the worst feelings, the worst.

00:04:28.571 --> 00:04:30.280
It's almost worst than failing,

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.585
'cause when you fail at least you know,

00:04:31.585 --> 00:04:33.947
"Heck, I can still find
a way to make it happen",

00:04:33.947 --> 00:04:36.039
but when you succeed and you're not happy,

00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:38.604
you're not fulfilled, then
you got a real problem.

00:04:38.604 --> 00:04:41.877
There's two things that control
everything in your life,

00:04:41.877 --> 00:04:44.757
every thought, every
feeling, every emotion,

00:04:44.757 --> 00:04:46.489
every action you have in your life,

00:04:46.489 --> 00:04:47.823
what you're wearing today,

00:04:47.823 --> 00:04:49.799
whether you're going to turn
this off within a few minutes

00:04:49.799 --> 00:04:51.169
or whether you're going to stick with me

00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:52.442
for two or three minutes,

00:04:52.442 --> 00:04:54.500
it's all controlled by two things:

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.283
your beliefs and your values.

00:04:57.283 --> 00:04:58.722
Whatever you believe, if you think life

00:04:58.722 --> 00:05:01.879
is just a waste of time,
doesn't matter what you do,

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:04.725
or you're big-boned, then, obviously,

00:05:04.725 --> 00:05:05.959
you're not going to go forth,

00:05:05.959 --> 00:05:06.823
you're not going to try to lose weight,

00:05:06.823 --> 00:05:08.604
you're not going to go
push for that next level

00:05:08.604 --> 00:05:10.184
with your career or your finances

00:05:10.184 --> 00:05:12.701
or your relationship or anything else.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:16.034
Beliefs control us, but so do our values.

00:05:16.034 --> 00:05:17.989
Some people, you know,
value just kicking back,

00:05:17.989 --> 00:05:20.012
some people value making it happen,

00:05:20.012 --> 00:05:21.886
some people value their family the most,

00:05:21.886 --> 00:05:23.501
some people value love.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:25.150
But you know what the real challenge is?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.976
When values are in conflict,

00:05:26.976 --> 00:05:28.866
when you really want to make
a difference in the world

00:05:28.866 --> 00:05:31.311
or you really want to do
wealth for your family,

00:05:31.311 --> 00:05:33.394
or you really want to do well financially,

00:05:33.394 --> 00:05:37.111
but simultaneously you
don't want to upset anybody,

00:05:37.111 --> 00:05:38.281
you want to be totally honest

00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:40.116
and you want to make everybody happy.

00:05:40.116 --> 00:05:42.575
When we have conflicts
between what we want

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.989
and what we think we can have,

00:05:43.989 --> 00:05:46.622
or you have a goal, what your
really want to make happen,

00:05:46.622 --> 00:05:49.491
but then you have this other
belief inside that says,

00:05:49.491 --> 00:05:51.676
"This damn stuff never does work".

00:05:51.676 --> 00:05:54.016
Those inner conflicts are what keep people

00:05:54.016 --> 00:05:55.336
from using all of their energy,

00:05:55.336 --> 00:05:57.038
it's kind of like taking two steps forward

00:05:57.038 --> 00:05:58.460
and three steps back.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.884
You know, it used to be
people kind of run on

00:05:59.884 --> 00:06:03.135
kind of seven-year cycles, it's
kind of an arbitrary number

00:06:03.135 --> 00:06:05.921
but think about it, from 17 to 24

00:06:05.921 --> 00:06:08.311
it's kind of stage a
life for a lot of people,

00:06:08.311 --> 00:06:12.478
from 24 really to about 31,
that's another stage of life,

00:06:13.371 --> 00:06:16.188
32 to 39 or 40 years old, another stage,

00:06:16.188 --> 00:06:18.384
40 to 47, another stage.

00:06:18.384 --> 00:06:21.006
And those are random
numbers, but what I mean is

00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:23.556
people tend to have an idea of
what they think life's about,

00:06:23.556 --> 00:06:25.346
"It's my kids. It's building my business".

00:06:25.346 --> 00:06:27.777
"It's making money.
It's God. It's family".

00:06:27.777 --> 00:06:29.997
Whatever it is, and then they go for it

00:06:29.997 --> 00:06:32.408
for a period of time, three,
four, five, six, seven years,

00:06:32.408 --> 00:06:34.638
whatever, maybe 10,
but then there's a time

00:06:34.638 --> 00:06:36.908
in which people begin to question,

00:06:36.908 --> 00:06:39.039
they begin to look at their
life and they begin to say,

00:06:39.039 --> 00:06:41.131
"Is this really what I want?"

00:06:41.131 --> 00:06:43.187
Have you found yourself at that any time?

00:06:43.187 --> 00:06:45.074
And then they do one of two things,

00:06:45.074 --> 00:06:48.055
they either recommit and they
go for another seven years

00:06:48.055 --> 00:06:49.286
and they take it to another level,

00:06:49.286 --> 00:06:51.145
or they make a strategic decision

00:06:51.145 --> 00:06:53.214
that shifts the direction of their life.

00:06:53.214 --> 00:06:56.220
Either way, your decision
control your destiny,

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.590
and if you don't choose,
that's a choice as well.

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:00.033
Some people just kind
of stay in the middle,

00:07:00.033 --> 00:07:03.505
in that lukewarm place, not
sure what they really want.

00:07:03.505 --> 00:07:05.295
So, this is kind of off the cuff,

00:07:05.295 --> 00:07:07.387
what I'm really trying to say to you is,

00:07:07.387 --> 00:07:09.601
maybe the question to ask is,

00:07:09.601 --> 00:07:11.630
"What I want my life to be today,

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.387
"and where am I really going?

00:07:13.387 --> 00:07:15.541
"What is my destiny?
What's going to fill me up?

00:07:15.541 --> 00:07:17.389
"What's going to give me
the meaning for my life?

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:19.063
"What's going to give me joy in my life,

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:21.446
"not just achievement but real enjoyment,

00:07:21.446 --> 00:07:23.554
"a sense of meaning and aliveness?"

00:07:23.554 --> 00:07:25.776
- Seven billion plus people on the planet,

00:07:25.776 --> 00:07:28.584
you're different than
every single one of them.

00:07:28.584 --> 00:07:31.332
There's a unique aspect
to your personality,

00:07:31.332 --> 00:07:34.806
your style, your intentions,
your actions, your habits,

00:07:34.806 --> 00:07:37.247
your beliefs, who you are,

00:07:37.247 --> 00:07:41.168
and the way that you think is
unique from everybody else.

00:07:41.168 --> 00:07:42.643
We can measure it by science,

00:07:42.643 --> 00:07:44.607
we can measure it by observation,

00:07:44.607 --> 00:07:46.784
we can measure it just by simply

00:07:46.784 --> 00:07:49.636
asking people basic questions to discover

00:07:49.636 --> 00:07:51.367
everyone's got their own opinion,

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.837
everyone's got their own world view.

00:07:53.837 --> 00:07:56.704
And because of that then we have to ask,

00:07:56.704 --> 00:08:00.435
"Well, am I living my life uniquely?

00:08:00.435 --> 00:08:03.626
"Am I expressing who I genuinely am?

00:08:03.626 --> 00:08:07.326
"Are my expression genuine
and authentic and spontaneous

00:08:07.326 --> 00:08:11.270
"to who I am as a person,
or am I living a facade?

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:14.403
"Am I trying to be somebody
else to please somebody else,

00:08:14.403 --> 00:08:17.282
"to gain acceptance or love over here,

00:08:17.282 --> 00:08:21.449
"or am I truly being true to
myself, to my unique self,

00:08:23.528 --> 00:08:26.256
"to the inner side of who I really am

00:08:26.256 --> 00:08:27.976
"and what I want to show to the world?"

00:08:27.976 --> 00:08:30.710
Because a lot of people
really struggle with this,

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:32.374
and the reason they start setting out

00:08:32.374 --> 00:08:33.802
to look for their purpose in their life is

00:08:33.802 --> 00:08:35.263
one day they wake up and they realize

00:08:35.263 --> 00:08:37.753
they're not living their life,

00:08:37.753 --> 00:08:38.996
they're living their parents' life,

00:08:38.996 --> 00:08:41.113
their professor's life,
their teacher's life.

00:08:41.113 --> 00:08:43.331
They're living the life their
society or their culture

00:08:43.331 --> 00:08:44.881
or the norms told them to live.

00:08:44.881 --> 00:08:47.299
One day they wake up and say, "Whoa!

00:08:47.299 --> 00:08:48.775
"Why have I conformed to the point

00:08:48.775 --> 00:08:51.023
"where I don't eve know who I am anymore?"

00:08:51.023 --> 00:08:52.963
And they start this journey, sometimes,

00:08:52.963 --> 00:08:53.972
to look for life's purpose

00:08:53.972 --> 00:08:57.476
'cause they're trying to find themselves.

00:08:57.476 --> 00:08:59.573
They're not looking for a big purpose,

00:08:59.573 --> 00:09:01.459
they're looking for themselves.

00:09:01.459 --> 00:09:03.058
And sometimes when we can tap back

00:09:03.058 --> 00:09:05.449
into that uniqueness of who we are,

00:09:05.449 --> 00:09:09.271
then the magic of life
comes alive again, you know?

00:09:09.271 --> 00:09:13.530
That requires us to not only
exude who you are to the world

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.492
but to genuinely express
who we are, what we think,

00:09:17.492 --> 00:09:20.572
what we desire of life, what we need.

00:09:20.572 --> 00:09:24.465
How we truly feel and think
about the people in our lives,

00:09:24.465 --> 00:09:25.975
the things that we are
doing with our lives,

00:09:25.975 --> 00:09:27.647
the places and directions we're going.

00:09:27.647 --> 00:09:29.912
We have to do that if we want to sense

00:09:29.912 --> 00:09:32.333
that full uniqueness of ourselves.

00:09:32.333 --> 00:09:34.800
And, often, it is by suppressing ourselves

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.590
that we begin to suffer,
and we have to again ask,

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.582
"Well, then, what is the
point of all of this?

00:09:40.582 --> 00:09:45.213
"Is it to live as a carbon
copy of everybody else,

00:09:45.213 --> 00:09:48.978
"or to fully, with full
intention and aliveness,

00:09:48.978 --> 00:09:52.020
"animate the best of
who you are uniquely?"

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:56.730
I think that you being
yourself is the grand purpose.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.285
- A brain tattoo I love sharing

00:09:58.285 --> 00:10:00.248
with my audience is this one:

00:10:00.248 --> 00:10:04.122
"A job is only just a job
if you see it as a job".

00:10:04.122 --> 00:10:07.622
And so, why would you lose the opportunity

00:10:09.524 --> 00:10:13.691
to leverage what you do
everyday to grow your happiness,

00:10:15.069 --> 00:10:17.079
to grow your energy,

00:10:17.079 --> 00:10:19.901
to allow you to release more
of your talents in the world,

00:10:19.901 --> 00:10:21.609
to allow you to help more people?

00:10:21.609 --> 00:10:26.099
Why would you miss that opportunity
by falling into the trap

00:10:26.099 --> 00:10:28.744
of thinking, "This is just my job.

00:10:28.744 --> 00:10:32.362
"I'm just getting up in the
morning, working nine to five,

00:10:32.362 --> 00:10:35.839
"going down to the coal mine every day"?

00:10:35.839 --> 00:10:37.812
And you could say, "Well, Robin,

00:10:37.812 --> 00:10:40.635
"this doesn't apply to me.

00:10:40.635 --> 00:10:43.362
"I just have an ordinary job".

00:10:43.362 --> 00:10:45.875
Well, I've got to tell
you, I've met taxi drivers

00:10:45.875 --> 00:10:48.767
who feel their work is
incredibly meaningful.

00:10:48.767 --> 00:10:51.738
I mean I was at LaGuardia and I remember

00:10:51.738 --> 00:10:54.493
being in a taxi cab, and the
man had this white shirt,

00:10:54.493 --> 00:10:58.684
and his cab was perfection,
and I said, you know,

00:10:58.684 --> 00:11:01.061
"Your attitude is great,
your passion is awesome,

00:11:01.061 --> 00:11:02.989
"your cab is perfect,

00:11:02.989 --> 00:11:06.224
"you've got this fresh
newspaper for me to read.

00:11:06.224 --> 00:11:09.148
"What is your psychology
that allows you to do this?"

00:11:09.148 --> 00:11:11.939
And he said, "Robin,
this is not a dirty job,

00:11:11.939 --> 00:11:13.190
"it's an important job.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.488
"I get to make a difference".

00:11:15.488 --> 00:11:18.736
I remember being in
Johannesburg meeting the janitor

00:11:18.736 --> 00:11:21.471
in the Johannesburg men's room or WC

00:11:21.471 --> 00:11:25.638
who worked like he was the
Elon Musk of what he did.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.020
He worked like Pavarotti sang.

00:11:33.413 --> 00:11:34.957
And so my point is simply this,

00:11:34.957 --> 00:11:38.547
it's really your choice
as to how you will view

00:11:38.547 --> 00:11:40.424
the work you do every day,

00:11:40.424 --> 00:11:43.996
and even in the most, quote,
unquote, "ordinary work"

00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:45.671
you could find gold.

00:11:45.671 --> 00:11:47.210
And if you connect with the gold,

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:48.604
you connect with the meaning.

00:11:48.604 --> 00:11:50.064
And if you connect with the meaning,

00:11:50.064 --> 00:11:51.403
you connect with your talent.

00:11:51.403 --> 00:11:52.755
And if you connect with your talent,

00:11:52.755 --> 00:11:54.279
you connect with the best within you.

00:11:54.279 --> 00:11:55.818
And if you connect with
the best within you,

00:11:55.818 --> 00:11:58.049
you go to work every day

00:11:58.049 --> 00:12:02.056
and you are this shining
star of world-class,

00:12:02.056 --> 00:12:04.744
and you become the
Picasso of your industry,

00:12:04.744 --> 00:12:07.620
and everything else takes care of itself.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:11.961
- I just can't explain
to everybody, like, clear

00:12:11.961 --> 00:12:16.128
when you figure out who you
are and do all that, you win.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:19.410
If you're great at painting, paint,

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:22.045
and hire a partner to be your salesperson.

00:12:22.045 --> 00:12:24.142
If somebody at 20 years old made me

00:12:24.142 --> 00:12:25.568
their business partner as a painter,

00:12:25.568 --> 00:12:28.319
they'd be the most famous
painter in the world.

00:12:28.319 --> 00:12:31.847
Yet, most painters want to be the salesman

00:12:31.847 --> 00:12:35.454
and businessman, and women,
as well as the painter,

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:36.867
and there's a problem.

00:12:36.867 --> 00:12:41.773
80% of painting, 90% of people
that are great at painting

00:12:41.773 --> 00:12:45.088
are artists, and don't
have the DNA to sale.

00:12:45.088 --> 00:12:48.078
And vice versa, all my sales
friends or business friends

00:12:48.078 --> 00:12:49.559
that want to start all these businesses

00:12:49.559 --> 00:12:53.861
around something creative,
I've bad news for you, joll,

00:12:53.861 --> 00:12:55.556
you know, you can be a great salesman

00:12:55.556 --> 00:12:58.838
but your pottery sucks (muted).

00:12:58.838 --> 00:13:00.176
And so that's that.

00:13:00.176 --> 00:13:04.098
So, like, and that's a very
funny analogy for the following:

00:13:04.098 --> 00:13:08.913
figure out who you are, don't
apologize for who you are,

00:13:08.913 --> 00:13:12.165
and then become even greater
than you naturally are

00:13:12.165 --> 00:13:13.498
at what you are.

00:13:14.541 --> 00:13:15.792
- [Man In Phone] I think too
many people give a (muted)

00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:17.683
what other people think
