or your uncle dies and there's no one

00:22:49.939 --> 00:22:51.343
to take over his junkyard,

00:22:51.343 --> 00:22:54.337
or your little brother starts
a freaking video conference.

00:22:54.337 --> 00:22:55.424
Just like your life now,

00:22:55.424 --> 00:22:56.710
adulthood will have all this tension

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:58.736
between ideals and practicality,

00:22:58.736 --> 00:23:00.971
and you'll have to
balance competing desires,

00:23:00.971 --> 00:23:02.478
and you don't have to do just one thing,

00:23:02.478 --> 00:23:03.895
you can be an Electrical Engineer

00:23:03.895 --> 00:23:06.060
who volunteers on archeological digs.

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:09.124
William Carlos Williams was
both a poet and a doctor.

00:23:09.124 --> 00:23:11.521
Julia Child, besides from
being an extraordinary chef

00:23:11.521 --> 00:23:14.304
was also a freaking spy
for the United States.

00:23:14.304 --> 00:23:16.181
I mean, heck, if you told my college self

00:23:16.181 --> 00:23:18.308
that I'd one day be a
novelist with a side gig

00:23:18.308 --> 00:23:21.386
of putting my mustachio face
on the torsos of strangers,

00:23:21.386 --> 00:23:23.423
I would have been dully surprised.

00:23:23.423 --> 00:23:25.644
And you studied organic fracking chemistry

00:23:25.644 --> 00:23:27.689
before writing songs about Harry Potter.

00:23:27.689 --> 00:23:30.803
So here is my advise: study
broadly and without fear,

00:23:30.803 --> 00:23:32.076
learn a language, if you can,

00:23:32.076 --> 00:23:33.647
because that will make
your life more interesting,

00:23:33.647 --> 00:23:34.848
read a little bit everyday,

00:23:34.848 --> 00:23:36.840
but, most importantly,
try to surround yourself

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:39.526
with people you like and
make cool stuff with them.

00:23:39.526 --> 00:23:40.771
In the end, at least in my experience,

00:23:40.771 --> 00:23:42.175
what you do isn't going to be

00:23:42.175 --> 00:23:45.302
nearly as interesting or
important as who you do it with.

00:23:45.302 --> 00:23:46.541
- A lot of people ask me,

00:23:46.541 --> 00:23:48.931
"How do I know what my true purpose is?"

00:23:48.931 --> 00:23:53.036
The answer is the difference
between a career and a calling.

00:23:53.036 --> 00:23:56.940
It's the difference between
satisfaction and fulfillment.

00:23:56.940 --> 00:24:01.211
It is the difference between
an interest and a passion.

00:24:01.211 --> 00:24:03.595
What is the difference between
an interest and a passion?

00:24:03.595 --> 00:24:04.428
So many people,

00:24:04.428 --> 00:24:06.534
they're interested in
this, interested in that,

00:24:06.534 --> 00:24:09.476
but, see, when you're
going to marry somebody

00:24:09.476 --> 00:24:11.194
you don't get down on one knee and say,

00:24:11.194 --> 00:24:15.361
"Baby, would you marry me?
I'm interested in you".

00:24:17.408 --> 00:24:18.976
No, no, you don't do that

00:24:18.976 --> 00:24:21.924
unless you want to get smacked
in the face and then left.

00:24:21.924 --> 00:24:26.254
You got to say, "Baby,
I'm passionate about you.

00:24:26.254 --> 00:24:30.062
"You complete me. I cannot
truly live this life

00:24:30.062 --> 00:24:33.062
"without you, without us, together".

00:24:34.146 --> 00:24:36.474
That's operating from the heart.

00:24:36.474 --> 00:24:39.490
And if you don't operate from
the heart I can guarantee

00:24:39.490 --> 00:24:43.213
you will live a life climbing a ladder,

00:24:43.213 --> 00:24:47.117
and if you get to the top you will realize

00:24:47.117 --> 00:24:50.334
that it was laying against the wrong wall.

00:24:50.334 --> 00:24:53.434
They say, "Never become too
good at something you hate

00:24:53.434 --> 00:24:56.476
"or they will make you do it
for the rest of your life".

00:24:56.476 --> 00:24:58.875
So, look, ask yourself
these three questions:

00:24:58.875 --> 00:25:00.711
What are your natural talents?

00:25:00.711 --> 00:25:02.794
What is something you enjoy doing?

00:25:02.794 --> 00:25:05.371
What is something that
you can't shut up about?

00:25:05.371 --> 00:25:07.891
You got to read, write and talk about it.

00:25:07.891 --> 00:25:09.995
That's how you get closer and closer

00:25:09.995 --> 00:25:12.034
to your mission or purpose in life.

00:25:12.034 --> 00:25:15.588
Still confused? Okay, so I
believe that the best teacher

00:25:15.588 --> 00:25:17.998
of how to live life is death.

00:25:17.998 --> 00:25:20.136
Legend has it that when
we're on our deathbed

00:25:20.136 --> 00:25:22.699
we will be visited by ghosts,

00:25:22.699 --> 00:25:25.044
these are the ghosts of our ideas, dreams,

00:25:25.044 --> 00:25:28.379
abilities, talents given to us by life.

00:25:28.379 --> 00:25:30.588
And if we never acted on that idea,

00:25:30.588 --> 00:25:32.345
never pursued that dream,

00:25:32.345 --> 00:25:33.970
never worked on those skills,

00:25:33.970 --> 00:25:37.107
used our voice or wrote that book,

00:25:37.107 --> 00:25:40.774
then those ghosts will
say, "We came to you,

00:25:41.667 --> 00:25:44.917
"and only you could have given us life,

00:25:46.015 --> 00:25:49.265
"but now we must die with you forever".

00:25:51.235 --> 00:25:53.363
So, ask yourself this
question, my friends,

00:25:53.363 --> 00:25:55.714
engage this thought experiment,

00:25:55.714 --> 00:25:58.881
if you had one year to live, 365 days,

00:26:00.721 --> 00:26:03.764
and whatever you chose to do

00:26:03.764 --> 00:26:07.931
you were guaranteed to
succeed at, what would you do?

00:26:11.179 --> 00:26:15.346
Chances all of that is what
you should be doing right now.

